# What NOT to ship to the builder.
#
# ⛔ THERE WAS NO .dockerignore AT ALL, so every deploy uploaded 2.8 GB across 31,236 files — the
# whole working tree, including 1.7 GB of Rust build artifacts the image never opens. Fly warns
# about it and then uploads it anyway. It has already bitten a sibling repo: a 440 MB context once
# crawled to the builder at 0.2 MB/s and the deploy had to be abandoned. A context this size is a
# deploy that fails on a bad connection, which is the worst time to discover it.
#
# ⛔ THE DOCKERFILE IS THE SPEC FOR THIS FILE. It does not `COPY .` — it names what it wants:
# package*.json, server.mjs, lib, public, onchain/target/idl, devnet-mints.json, tools. Anything
# else is dead weight. So when the Dockerfile starts copying something new, it has to be allowed
# through here or the build breaks on a missing path.

# Build artifacts, 1.7 GB of it. The image needs the IDL out of onchain/ and NOTHING else, so
# exclude the directory's contents and then put the one needed path back.
#
# ⛔ `onchain` on its own would NOT work: excluding a directory by name prunes it before a later
# `!` can reach inside, so the re-include below would silently do nothing and
# `COPY onchain/target/idl` would fail. The `/*` form matches each child individually, which is
# what makes the exception possible. Keep both halves of each pair.
onchain/*
!onchain/target
onchain/target/*
!onchain/target/idl

# Installed in the image by `npm ci`, and these are macOS-native builds — shipping them would
# overwrite correct linux binaries with ones that cannot run.
node_modules
onchain/node_modules

# 392 MB of history. The commit is passed in as the GIT_SHA build arg instead.
.git
.gitignore

# Runtime state. The container mounts a Fly volume at DATA_DIR=/data; a local copy would be shadowed
# by the mount anyway, and it can hold real user data that has no business in an image layer.
data

# ⛔ Secrets must never enter an image: layers are readable by anyone who can pull it, and deleting
# a file in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier one. Fly secrets are injected as env.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
si-vault-key.json
**/id.json

# Not used at runtime: the deploy scripts themselves, CI config, and the on-chain test harness.
scripts
.github

# Local noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
